  "name": "Secondary Target",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Archer 14</p><p>The archer's incredible skill with bows or crossbows means that even failure is success. Whenever the archer misses his target with a ranged attack, he may redirect the attack to an enemy within 20 feet of his target. He makes an attack roll against the new target, and if successful, hits as if he had targeted them in the first place. The archer may use this ability as often as he misses, but once he hits a creature with a redirected attack, he cannot target it again this way until the beginning of his next turn.</p>",
